  "result": "Rebase when branch is shared only if everyone agrees to it. Default: merge.\n\n**Rebase OK when:**\n- Your local, unpushed commits: rebase onto updated base (`git pull --rebase`) for clean linear history.\n- Team agreed on rebase workflow and force-push coordination (`git push --force-with-lease`).\n- Cleaning up your own WIP commits before the branch merges.\n\n**Use merge when:**\n- Others have pulled or based work on the branch. Rebase rewrites commit hashes, so their history diverges and they get duplicate commits or conflicts.\n- You want to preserve true history and avoid force-push.\n\nRule: never rebase commits others already have.",
